<title>NORWAY: PGS orders two seismic ships for 1 bln NOK.</title>
<headline>PGS orders two seismic ships for 1 bln NOK.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian offshore company Petroleum Geo Services ASA has ordered two Ramford-style seismic survey ships from a local shipyard at a cost of about one billion crowns, investment group RGI said on Monday.</p>
<p>The contract went to Langsten Slip &amp; Baatbyggeri AS, which is unlisted by owned to 67.5 percent by RGI, an RGI official said.</p>
<p>The ships will be delivered in the first quarter of 1998.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
